course: dictionary
lesson: 3589
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which meaning the writer means. This is context. «Stop fiddling with your pencil» is not about music, because a pencil cannot play a tune. Fiddling here means touching or moving something, often because you are bored or nervous.
explain: «The fiddle played a lively jig at the ceilidh.» The words played, jig and ceilidh are your clues. A fiddle must be an instrument, a violin. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
explain: Some phrases use the word in a new way. «Fit as a fiddle» does not mean a violin at all. It means very healthy. Context and common phrases both help you work out an unfamiliar meaning.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Fiddle» can mean a violin, especially when it is used for folk or country music.
fact: «Fiddle with» something means to keep touching or moving it, often because you are nervous or bored.
fact: «Fiddle» can also mean to cheat, as in «fiddle the books», so always check the context.
fact: «Fit as a fiddle» means very healthy, and «play second fiddle» means to be less important.
exercise: «Stop fiddling with your pencil.» What does fiddling mean here? | To sing loudly | *To keep touching or moving something | To cheat | To play music on a violin
exercise: «He was fit as a fiddle after his long holiday.» What does fit as a fiddle mean? | *Very healthy | Very angry | Very small | Very tired
exercise: «The fiddle played a lively jig at the ceilidh.» Find and copy the word that tells you the fiddle is a musical instrument. | jig | fiddle | *played | lively
test: The news says «fiddling expenses» in a report about money. What does fiddling mean in that phrase? | Keeping very still | Being very healthy | Playing a violin | *Cheating
test: Which word describes a task that is awkward and needs careful, fiddly work? | *Fiddly | Fit | Ancient | Lively
exam: The story that Nero played the fiddle while Rome burned is a myth; the fiddle had not even been invented. What does this tell you? | *The story cannot be true, because the instrument did not exist yet | The fiddle was very old and famous in Rome | Rome was built by fiddle players | Nero was a famous fiddle maker
